, "width": 44.700000000000045, "height": 67.20000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Mapped antisense to gene (%) 15.9", "bbox": {"x": 1408.7, "y": 751.5, "width": 125.29999999999995, "height": 115.10000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "35.4", "bbox": {"x": 1409.2, "y": 882.6, "width": 44.700000000000045, "height": 22.399999999999977}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "17.7", "bbox": {"x": 1409.2, "y": 920.9, "width": 41.5, "height": 25.600000000000023}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "4.1", "bbox": {"x": 1412.4, "y": 962.5, "width": 32.0, "height": 19.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "9.4", "bbox": {"x": 1412.4, "y": 1000.9, "width": 32.0, "height": 19.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "33.7 19.4 12.7", "bbox": {"x": 1409.2, "y": 1039.0, "width": 44.700000000000045, "height": 106.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "which showed mast cell activation, gastric acid secretion, molecular mediation of the inflammatory response, and Fc-e receptor signalling pathways (Fig S4).", "bbox": {"x": 131.0, "y": 1646.8, "width": 696.5999999999999, "height": 93.20000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Discussion", "bbox": {"x": 134.2, "y": 1825.9, "width": 175.8, "height": 35.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Here, we have demonstrated a practical and effective method of isolating nuclei from human skeletal muscle. Our method yields sufficient quantities of nuclei for snRNAseq. In total, 43,325 nuclei were recovered. With this method, we identified 12 distinct cell", "bbox": {"x": 134.2, "y": 1899.0, "width": 696.5999999999999, "height": 122.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "types which are consistent with previous reports in human skeletal muscle (De Micheli et al, 2020; Rubenstein et al, 2020; Orchard et al, 2021). Notably, this included a large proportion of type I and type II myonuclei. To our knowledge, there have been only a few reports of successfully isolating human myonuclei in significant quantities (Orchard et al, 2021; Eraslan et al, 2022; Scripture-Adams et al, 2022). Importantly, we were able to obtain consistent quality control metrics from a variety of samples. This included muscle representing both sexes, collected from the commonly biopsied deltoid and vastus lateralis muscles, and from patients from 33 up to 64 yr of age. In addition, the biopsy from patient M2 was performed in 2006 and still yielded 4,000 nuclei (Table 1), suggesting that this", "bbox": {"x": 872.3, "y": 1643.4, "width": 693.6000000000001, "height": 380.6999999999998}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "snRNAseq protocol for frozen muscle tissues Soule et al.", "bbox": {"x": 134.1, "y": 2095.0, "width": 508.4, "height": 26.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "https:/ / doi.org/10.26508 / lsa.202201806", "bbox": {"x": 875.6, "y": 2097.7, "width": 338.69999999999993, "height": 22.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "vol 6 | no 5 | e202201806", "bbox": {"x": 1220.7, "y": 2097.7, "width": 230.0999999999999, "height": 19.300000000000182}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "3 of 11", "bbox": {"x": 1501.9, "y": 2097.7, "width": 60.700000000000045, "height": 19.300000000000182}}], "ms": 311.72}